<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Sept industry output falls 1.8 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Sept industry output falls 1.8 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT Sept 96     Aug 96     Sept 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   -1.8	 unch	 +1.0</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     -1.5	 +1.3	 +0.7</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		97.5	 99.3	 99.0</p>
<p>NOTE - The ministry said the September index was likely to be revised upward. &quot;Experience shows the preliminary September data will be corrected upward significantly,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				   Sept 96		   Aug 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining			73.8	+1.1	73.0	 -2.0</p>
<p> Manufacturing output    95.6	-2.2	97.8	+0.6</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods   100.5	-1.1     101.6	+1.3</p>
<p>	Capital goods	92.8	-2.6	95.3	-0.9</p>
<p>	Consumer durables  83.2	-9.3	91.7	+4.1</p>
<p>	Consumer goods     95.9	-0.7	96.6	unch</p>
<p> Energy output	    103.0	-3.7     107.0	+0.5</p>
<p> Construction	     117.4	+2.5     114.5	-4.9 @</p>
<p>Two month comparison Aug/Sept 96 with June/July 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     -0.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing output		  -0.5</p>
<p> Construction			    -1.0</p>
<p> Capital goods			   -2.0</p>
<p> Mining				    -3.0</p>
<p> Energy output			   -1.5</p>
<p> Consumer durables and goods	 -0.5</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +1.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison Aug/Sept 1996 with Aug/Sept 1995:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     -0.8</p>
<p> Mining				    -8.9</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 +0.1</p>
<p>  Incl: Intermediate goods	   -0.1</p>
<p>	  Capital goods		  -0.1</p>
<p>	  Consumer durables	    +3.9</p>
<p>	  Consumer goods		 -1.3</p>
<p> Energy output			   +2.2</p>
<p> Construction			    -5.9</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
